WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.401 --> 00:00:04.003
Republicans are already
signaling their intent

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:06.239
to stonewall
President Biden's agenda

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:08.808
while dismissing the need
for an impeachment trial

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:10.243
for former President Trump.

00:00:10.243 --> 00:00:13.012
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:13.012 --> 00:00:15.982
[ Theme music plays ]

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:17.483
Our political system

00:00:17.483 --> 00:00:20.119
is currently overloaded
way beyond its capacity.

00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:23.156
It's like a power strip with
way too many things plugged in.

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:25.691
We already got the TV, Roku,
printer, modem,

00:00:25.691 --> 00:00:27.760
iPad, InstaPod,
immersion blender,

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:29.562
Christmas tree, and toaster
plugged in,

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:32.364
and now we need to find room
for the sleep-apnea machine.

00:00:32.364 --> 00:00:36.235
And because I live in New York,
there's only one other outlet,

00:00:36.235 --> 00:00:37.670
and it was drywalled over

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.405
during
the Coolidge administration,

00:00:39.405 --> 00:00:42.575 line:0%
on top of a deadly pandemic
that has overwhelmed hospitals,

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:44.744 line:0%
an unprecedented
economic collapse

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:46.812 line:0%
that has plunged millions
into joblessness

00:00:46.812 --> 00:00:49.415 line:0%
and food scarcity and
a botched vaccine rollout

00:00:49.415 --> 00:00:51.884 line:0%
that has states saying they're
about to run out of doses,

00:00:51.884 --> 00:00:54.520
we also have a violent
authoritarian movement

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:56.155
that tried to
overthrow democracy,

00:00:56.155 --> 00:00:58.524
led by a former president
facing an impeachment trial

00:00:58.524 --> 00:01:00.826
for, um --
What was it for, again?

00:01:00.826 --> 00:01:03.462 line:53%
-There will be a trial,
and when that trial ends,

00:01:03.462 --> 00:01:06.933 line:53%
Senators will have to decide
if they believe

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:11.204 line:53%
Donald John Trump
incited the erection --

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:15.274 line:53%
insurrection against
the United States.

00:01:15.274 --> 00:01:17.510
-Well, if erection
is the charge,

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:20.513
then we certainly
don't want him to beat it.

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:23.583
-♪ Yeah ♪

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:26.585
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.585 --> 00:01:29.055
-And they thought we were gonna
run out of material.

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:31.791
They should do
a "CSI: Mar-a-Lago."

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:33.059
Shut up!

00:01:33.059 --> 00:01:36.362
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:38.565
Who needs you
rolling your eyes at me?

00:01:38.565 --> 00:01:41.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.969
The only bummer
about Schumer's gaffe was

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:45.037
it happened on a Friday,
when we were dark,

00:01:45.037 --> 00:01:47.807
so the only person I could tell
my "beat it" joke to

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:49.542
was my wife,
but she bought

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:51.644
noise-canceling headphones

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:55.348
on our honeymoon
seven years ago.

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:58.050
Anyway, today the White House
officially sent --

00:01:58.050 --> 00:01:59.985
excuse me -- today
the House officially sent --

00:01:59.985 --> 00:02:02.388
still not as bad as
"erection"/"insurrection."

00:02:02.388 --> 00:02:04.156
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.156 --> 00:02:07.193
But a reminder,
we all make mistakes, Chuck.

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:09.495
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.495 --> 00:02:12.097
Anyway, today the House
officially sent

00:02:12.097 --> 00:02:14.167
its article of impeachment
over to the Senate,

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:16.302
setting up a trial in two weeks.

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:19.538 line:68%
-The Historic second impeachment
of President Trump

00:02:19.538 --> 00:02:21.808 line:71%
that takes a big step forward.

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:23.543 line:68%
The one article
brought against him,

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:25.144 line:71%
incitement of insurrection,

00:02:25.144 --> 00:02:26.746 line:71%
will be delivered to the Senate.

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:28.581 line:71%
That triggers a Senate trial,

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:30.383 line:68%
now set to begin
in about two weeks.

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:32.585 line:53%
-Monday is that day
that Pelosi and the House

00:02:32.585 --> 00:02:35.754
will formally transmit
that one article of impeachmemt

00:02:35.754 --> 00:02:37.990
to the Senate,
kicking off Tuesday

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:40.126
as the day where Senators
will be sworn in

00:02:40.126 --> 00:02:42.128
as members of the trial.

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:44.230
But then it will be
another two weeks

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:47.166
until we see that trial
formally begin.

00:02:47.166 --> 00:02:48.668
McConnell actually arguing

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:50.270
he actually wanted three weeks

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:52.671 line:53%
so that the president
could actually begin

00:02:52.671 --> 00:02:54.874 line:57%
to create his defense team

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:57.876 line:53%
and also strengthen his argument
against impeachment.

00:02:57.876 --> 00:02:59.879
-So, Trump's lawyers
will have two weeks

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:02.248
to prepare for their defense,
which I guess will be --

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:05.618
what? -- when he told the
violent mob of unhinged rioters

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:08.454
to march down to the Capitol
and fight to stop Democrats

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:10.990
from stealing the election,
he was joking?

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:13.793
"Your Honor, when he whipped the
insurrectionists into a frenzy,

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:15.060
he was being sarcastic.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:16.696
That's why he turned
to the camera,

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:19.065
and made
a freeze-frame sitcom face,

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:21.433
the classic Mr. Roper Defense.

00:03:21.433 --> 00:03:23.636
Not to be confused
with Furley's Gambit.

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:26.538
Or maybe they'll say
it was a different guy.

00:03:26.538 --> 00:03:29.975
"Ya got the wrong Donald Trump.
You want this guy."

00:03:29.975 --> 00:03:32.878 line:57%
-You have an opportunity today!

00:03:32.878 --> 00:03:39.418 line:53%
You can be a hero,
or you can be a zero!

00:03:39.418 --> 00:03:41.521
-This is like where you're
in a conference room

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:43.589
at a Radisson,
listening to a life coach

00:03:43.589 --> 00:03:45.158
tell you how to pick up women.

00:03:45.158 --> 00:03:48.394
"You can be a hero,
or you can be a zero!

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:52.899
You could be a single guy,
or you can be the mingle guy!

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:57.971
You can be a dud and a chump,
or you can be a stud on a stump!

00:03:57.971 --> 00:04:00.106
Yeah, I posed for that picture!"

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:01.707
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.707 --> 00:04:03.976
Don Jr. has so much confidence
onstage.

00:04:03.976 --> 00:04:05.745
But I bet if you'd
try to find him after,

00:04:05.745 --> 00:04:07.179
and tell him he did a great job,

00:04:07.179 --> 00:04:10.015
he'll be leaning against
the wall, smoking and crying.

00:04:10.015 --> 00:04:13.052
"Do you think my dad just narked
me out to the feds?!"

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:15.088
Of course, Trump has had
a little trouble

00:04:15.088 --> 00:04:17.323
assembling a defense team
for his impeachment,

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:20.159
because his usual lawyer is busy
getting sued

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:22.962
for over a billion dollars.

00:04:22.962 --> 00:04:26.899 line:68%
-"The New York Times" reports
that Dominion Voting Systems

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:30.068 line:68%
has filed a defamation lawsuit
this morning

00:04:30.068 --> 00:04:32.505 line:71%
against Rudy Giuliani.

00:04:32.505 --> 00:04:36.042 line:68%
According to the paper,
the 107-page lawsuit

00:04:36.042 --> 00:04:39.145 line:68%
accuses Mr. Giuliani
of carrying out

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:42.682 line:68%
a viral disinformation campaign
about Dominion,

00:04:42.682 --> 00:04:46.051 line:68%
made up of demonstrably false
allegations,

00:04:46.051 --> 00:04:48.587 line:71%
in part, to enrich himself

00:04:48.587 --> 00:04:51.590 line:68%
through legal fees
and his podcast.

00:04:51.590 --> 00:04:57.897 line:68%
The suit seeks damages of
more than $1.3 billion.

00:04:57.897 --> 00:05:00.933
-It's funny, if you sue someone
for a billion dollars,

00:05:00.933 --> 00:05:02.235
it sound like a joke.

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:04.937
But when you sue them
for $1.3 billion,

00:05:04.937 --> 00:05:07.205
you start to think, "Oh, they
might have some evidence."

00:05:07.205 --> 00:05:09.975
What are you gonna do,
sue me for a billion dollars?

00:05:09.975 --> 00:05:13.379
Oh, $1.3 billion?
What do they know?"

00:05:13.379 --> 00:05:14.647
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:16.782
And $1.3 billion from Rudy?!

00:05:16.782 --> 00:05:18.617
Good thing
vampires are immortal,

00:05:18.617 --> 00:05:20.486
because he'll have work
the rest of his life

00:05:20.486 --> 00:05:21.620
to pay that off.

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:23.856
I mean, he doesn't have
any money.

00:05:23.856 --> 00:05:25.924
This poor man
doesn't have any money.

00:05:25.924 --> 00:05:28.060
Do you remember how he couldn't
even afford hair dye

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:30.996
and just rubbed
a typewriter ribbon on his head?

00:05:30.996 --> 00:05:34.433
Plus, he's probably still
playing alimony to his cousin.

00:05:34.433 --> 00:05:37.603
[ Laughter ]

00:05:37.603 --> 00:05:40.106
Trump reportedly
won't even pay Rudy

00:05:40.106 --> 00:05:42.008
for all those trips he made
across the country,

00:05:42.008 --> 00:05:43.476
lying to steal the election,

00:05:43.476 --> 00:05:45.410
and I'm betting
Trump made him fly cheap.

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:48.514
Rudy probably had to buy
a wing seat on Spirit Airlines.

00:05:48.514 --> 00:05:50.249
[ Lisping ] I talk like this

00:05:50.249 --> 00:05:52.818
because my teeth
are still full of bugs.

00:05:52.818 --> 00:05:54.554
[ Normal voice ] Of course,
Trump isn't actually defending
--

00:05:54.554 --> 00:05:56.122
excuse me -- depending on --

00:05:56.122 --> 00:05:58.090
I'm really Schumer-ing it up.

00:05:58.090 --> 00:06:00.726
[ Laughter ]

00:06:00.726 --> 00:06:03.262
Chuck Schumer --
Chuck Schumer cursed me.

00:06:03.262 --> 00:06:05.364
Now who is laughing?

00:06:05.364 --> 00:06:07.233
-♪ Yeah ♪

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:10.503
[ Laughter ]

00:06:13.306 --> 00:06:15.942
I love when we cut out right
before we have to pay The Who.

00:06:15.942 --> 00:06:17.109
[ Laughter ]

00:06:17.109 --> 00:06:19.145
You know who owns
the publishing for The Who?

00:06:19.145 --> 00:06:20.580
Ol' Rolex Wally.

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:23.416
-♪ Yeah ♪

00:06:23.416 --> 00:06:26.052
-Three seconds.
We don't owe you a dime!

00:06:26.052 --> 00:06:28.587
[ Laughter ]

00:06:28.587 --> 00:06:31.223
Of course, Trump isn't actually
depending on a real defense

00:06:31.223 --> 00:06:33.826
of his actions, because they're
obviously indefensible.

00:06:33.826 --> 00:06:35.828
I'm no lawyer,
but it's pretty obvious

00:06:35.828 --> 00:06:37.029
he tried to commit sedition,

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:38.798
he fomented
a violent insurrection

00:06:38.798 --> 00:06:40.533
to stop the lawful counting
of electoral votes,

00:06:40.533 --> 00:06:42.634
nearly installed a crony
at the Department of Justice

00:06:42.634 --> 00:06:44.069
to overturn the results,

00:06:44.069 --> 00:06:45.938
and tried to bully
the Secretary of State

00:06:45.938 --> 00:06:47.806
in Georgia
to commit election fraud.

00:06:47.806 --> 00:06:49.408
What Trump is
really depending on

00:06:49.408 --> 00:06:52.678
is servile, morally bankrupt
Republicans falling in line.

00:06:52.678 --> 00:06:54.713
And judging from comments
they made over the weekend,

00:06:54.713 --> 00:06:56.715
the GOP is fully on board.

00:06:56.715 --> 00:06:59.385 line:68%
-This election was not stolen.
Do you accept that fact?

00:07:02.588 --> 00:07:04.857 line:68%
-Well, what I would say is
that the debate

00:07:04.857 --> 00:07:07.193 line:68%
over whether or not
there was fraud should occur.

00:07:07.193 --> 00:07:09.928 line:68%
-The Department of Justice,
led by William Barr,

00:07:09.928 --> 00:07:12.131 line:68%
said there is no widespread
evidence of fraud.

00:07:12.131 --> 00:07:13.665 line:71%
Can't you just say the words

00:07:13.665 --> 00:07:15.100 line:68%
that the election
was not stolen?

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:18.370 line:68%
-What I would suggest is --
What I would suggest is

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:20.806 line:68%
that if we want greater
confidence in our elections --

00:07:20.806 --> 00:07:23.643 line:68%
and 75% of Republicans
agree with me --

00:07:23.643 --> 00:07:26.645 line:68%
is that we do need to look
at election integrity.

00:07:26.645 --> 00:07:28.948 line:15%
-If you listen to what the
president said at the rally,

00:07:28.948 --> 00:07:31.717 line:15%
he said,
"Demonstrate peacefully."

00:07:31.717 --> 00:07:33.218 line:21%
And then I got a question later

00:07:33.218 --> 00:07:35.221 line:15%
about whether
did he incite them.

00:07:35.221 --> 00:07:37.723 line:15%
I also think everybody
across this country

00:07:37.723 --> 00:07:39.224 line:21%
has some responsibility.

00:07:39.224 --> 00:07:41.861 line:53%
-I think the trial is stupid.
I think it's counterproductive.

00:07:41.861 --> 00:07:44.029 line:60%
I think this is gonna be
really bad for the country.

00:07:44.029 --> 00:07:45.764 line:60%
It's going take us --
Not just is it going to

00:07:45.764 --> 00:07:47.733 line:60%
keep us from focusing
on really important things,

00:07:47.733 --> 00:07:50.402 line:60%
but it's also just going to
stir it up even more.

00:07:50.402 --> 00:07:52.337
-Man, they're throwing
everything at the wall --

00:07:52.337 --> 00:07:53.906
impeachment
will stir up the country;

00:07:53.906 --> 00:07:56.408
the election was stolen;
we all bear some responsibility.

00:07:56.408 --> 00:07:57.810
It's like getting pulled over

00:07:57.810 --> 00:07:59.978
with a giant plume
of marijuana smoke in the car

00:07:59.978 --> 00:08:01.880
and telling the cop,
"I think it's the exhaust pipe.

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:03.849
It is legal in several states.

00:08:03.849 --> 00:08:05.885
And I only started smoking
when you pulled me over,

00:08:05.885 --> 00:08:07.619
because that gave me
severe anxiety."

00:08:07.619 --> 00:08:10.088
Also, Marco, honestly,
do you have any shame at all?

00:08:10.088 --> 00:08:11.591
You called Trump
an embarrassment

00:08:11.591 --> 00:08:13.926
and a con man
and implied in public

00:08:13.926 --> 00:08:15.328
that he had a tiny [Bleep].

00:08:15.328 --> 00:08:17.129
But now you're
calling impeachment stupid?

00:08:17.129 --> 00:08:19.898
Also, you famously doinked a kid
in the head with a football.

00:08:19.898 --> 00:08:22.101
You don't get to call anything
stupid after that, ever.

00:08:22.101 --> 00:08:24.269
And you think impeachment
would stir up the country?

00:08:24.269 --> 00:08:25.538
It's already stirred.

00:08:25.538 --> 00:08:26.972
This is what you call "stirred."

00:08:26.972 --> 00:08:28.607
You guys already
did the stirring.

00:08:28.607 --> 00:08:30.443
You don't get to pretend
everything is just fine now.

00:08:30.443 --> 00:08:32.511
Violent seditionists
and white supremacists

00:08:32.511 --> 00:08:34.613
and militia members
stormed the Capitol building

00:08:34.613 --> 00:08:35.848
and tried
to overthrow democracy.

00:08:35.848 --> 00:08:36.949
We have to
do something about that

00:08:36.949 --> 00:08:38.384
so it doesn't happen again.

00:08:38.384 --> 00:08:41.186
Instead, Republican leaders
are talking about Trump's base

00:08:41.186 --> 00:08:44.256
the way park rangers talk
about bears on a campground.

00:08:44.256 --> 00:08:47.259
"Don't make eye contact,
move away slowly,

00:08:47.259 --> 00:08:50.563
and if worse comes to worse,
let them eat your hot dogs.

00:08:50.563 --> 00:08:52.231
They're just hot dogs."

00:08:52.231 --> 00:08:53.999
So Republicans have already
made it clear

00:08:53.999 --> 00:08:55.634
they refuse
to hold Trump accountable

00:08:55.634 --> 00:08:57.937
for inciting an insurrection
or do anything at all

00:08:57.937 --> 00:08:59.672
about the violent
authoritarian movement

00:08:59.672 --> 00:09:02.107
they've cultivated,
not to mention the pandemic,

00:09:02.107 --> 00:09:04.610
vaccine rollout,
and economic crisis.

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:07.646
Suffice it to say, just because
Joe Biden is president now

00:09:07.646 --> 00:09:09.115
doesn't mean
things are normal again.

00:09:09.115 --> 00:09:10.282
They're not.
At this point,

00:09:10.282 --> 00:09:11.750
when I check my phone
in the morning,

00:09:11.750 --> 00:09:13.919
I just have one news alert
from CNN

00:09:13.919 --> 00:09:15.587
that says,
"Breaking: everything."

00:09:15.587 --> 00:09:19.224
Nearly a million people have
recently filed for unemployment,

00:09:19.224 --> 00:09:20.626
thousands are dying a day,

00:09:20.626 --> 00:09:22.561
and the one thing
that could be a silver bullet,

00:09:22.561 --> 00:09:23.829
distribution of the vaccine,

00:09:23.829 --> 00:09:26.031
was left in disarray
by the last administration.

00:09:26.031 --> 00:09:28.934
In fact, millions of doses
are reportedly missing,

00:09:28.934 --> 00:09:31.470
and no one knows why
or where they are.

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:33.072
For all we know, Trump
left the White House

00:09:33.072 --> 00:09:35.174
with a bunch of vials
stuffed in his coat,

00:09:35.174 --> 00:09:37.643 line:0%
and now he's selling them
at the Mar-a-Lago buffet.

00:09:37.643 --> 00:09:39.044
I don't even know
where to begin

00:09:39.044 --> 00:09:40.579
when I check the news
in the morning.

00:09:40.579 --> 00:09:42.882
I open my "New York Times" app,
and all the headlines are bad,

00:09:42.882 --> 00:09:44.249
so I check
"The Washington Post" app,

00:09:44.249 --> 00:09:45.551
and all the headlines are bad.

00:09:45.551 --> 00:09:47.319
And then I check the
"Pittsburgh Post-Gazette" app,

00:09:47.319 --> 00:09:49.655
and the Steelers
are still out of the playoff.

00:09:49.655 --> 00:09:51.791 line:60%
Which reminds me, last week,
after Ted Cruz said

00:09:51.791 --> 00:09:53.826 line:60%
President Biden was choosing
the people of Paris

00:09:53.826 --> 00:09:56.261 line:60%
over the people of Pittsburgh,
I favorably compared

00:09:56.261 --> 00:09:58.130
my father's hometown of
Pittsburgh to Paris,

00:09:58.130 --> 00:09:59.965
remarking that,
unlike Pittsburgh,

00:09:59.965 --> 00:10:01.767
Paris doesn't have an incline.

00:10:01.767 --> 00:10:03.768
Well, some French viewers
were quick to point out

00:10:03.768 --> 00:10:05.137
that Paris does, in fact,

00:10:05.137 --> 00:10:07.473
have an incline, or funicular,
in Montmartre.

00:10:07.473 --> 00:10:09.642
So I would like to retract
that statement.

00:10:09.642 --> 00:10:13.511
I also called Ted Cruz a jagoff,
and I'd like to retract that,

00:10:13.511 --> 00:10:16.248
but only so that I can say it
again for the first time.

00:10:16.248 --> 00:10:18.551
Ted Cruz, you're a jagoff.

00:10:18.551 --> 00:10:20.653
On top of everything else
that's going on right now,

00:10:20.653 --> 00:10:22.254
there are also the crises
that preceded Trump,

00:10:22.254 --> 00:10:24.289
like our healthcare crisis,
the climate crisis,

00:10:24.289 --> 00:10:26.524
voter suppression,
structural inequality

00:10:26.524 --> 00:10:29.028
and institutional racism,
not to mention the conditions

00:10:29.028 --> 00:10:31.429
that nearly allowed Trump
to remain in office

00:10:31.429 --> 00:10:33.032
or steal the election,

00:10:33.032 --> 00:10:35.835
despite winning
7 million fewer votes.

00:10:35.835 --> 00:10:39.004
We need mechanisms in place
for bold systemic change

00:10:39.004 --> 00:10:40.906
and immediate relief
for suffering Americans,

00:10:40.906 --> 00:10:42.508
which is why
the Biden administration

00:10:42.508 --> 00:10:45.978
has started by offering a plan
to provide billions of dollars

00:10:45.978 --> 00:10:49.148
for vaccine distribution,
increased unemployment benefits,

00:10:49.148 --> 00:10:51.717
direct payments,
and a $15 minimum wage,

00:10:51.717 --> 00:10:53.752
among other things.
Republicans meanwhile

00:10:53.752 --> 00:10:56.689
have responded by announcing
their opposition to it.

00:10:56.689 --> 00:11:00.659 line:68%
-President Joe Biden's proposal
to boost the U.S. economy

00:11:00.659 --> 00:11:03.195 line:68%
and efforts to fight
the COVID-19 pandemic

00:11:03.195 --> 00:11:05.931 line:68%
is facing
some Republican opposition.

00:11:05.931 --> 00:11:07.133 line:64%
-While Biden is pushing

00:11:07.133 --> 00:11:08.901 line:60%
for Republican and Democratic
lawmakers

00:11:08.901 --> 00:11:10.603 line:64%
to work toward an agreement,

00:11:10.603 --> 00:11:13.105 line:60%
there's some criticism
from the GOP.

00:11:13.105 --> 00:11:14.673 line:0%
-Multiple
Congressional Republicans,

00:11:14.673 --> 00:11:17.609 line:0%
from Senator Pat Toomey
to Congressman Kevin Brady,

00:11:17.609 --> 00:11:19.712 line:0%
top Republican on the House
Ways and Means Committee,

00:11:19.712 --> 00:11:23.081 line:0%
have public panned Biden's
proposal as a nonstarter.

00:11:23.081 --> 00:11:25.117 line:53%
-Republican Senator
Susan Collins,

00:11:25.117 --> 00:11:27.719 line:53%
who was on the call,
has reservations,

00:11:27.719 --> 00:11:30.756 line:53%
writing in a statement,
"It seems premature

00:11:30.756 --> 00:11:33.826 line:53%
to be considering a package
of this size and scope."

00:11:33.826 --> 00:11:36.529
-I'm sorry, Susan Collins, it's
premature?

00:11:36.529 --> 00:11:38.197
You want to wait a little longer

00:11:38.197 --> 00:11:39.698
and see how much worse
things can get?

00:11:39.698 --> 00:11:42.133
This is like if the Steelers
waited a couple more weeks

00:11:42.133 --> 00:11:43.702
to find a running game.
Okay.

00:11:43.702 --> 00:11:47.573
Okay, now I get why my wife
bought those headphones.

00:11:47.573 --> 00:11:48.941
I just heard it.

00:11:48.941 --> 00:11:50.342
I just heard it
for the first time.

00:11:50.342 --> 00:11:51.844
Seriously, when would be
the right time

00:11:51.844 --> 00:11:53.244
to maybe start thinking
about considering

00:11:53.244 --> 00:11:54.813
possibly doing something
eventually

00:11:54.813 --> 00:11:57.049
about the highly infectious
virus rapidly spreading

00:11:57.049 --> 00:11:58.917
across the country,
overwhelming hospitals,

00:11:58.917 --> 00:12:00.318
and forcing millions
out of work?

00:12:00.318 --> 00:12:01.987
When would be
a good time for you?

00:12:01.987 --> 00:12:03.388
Getting these people
to do something

00:12:03.388 --> 00:12:04.757
about a national crisis is like

00:12:04.757 --> 00:12:06.858
getting Verizon to come
set up your Fios.

00:12:06.858 --> 00:12:09.428
"We could pencil you in
sometime between 9:00 a.m.

00:12:09.428 --> 00:12:12.531
and 6:00 p.m. on Saturday,
March 37, 2045.

00:12:12.531 --> 00:12:13.999
Would that work?
Can you give us your address

00:12:13.999 --> 00:12:15.967
to the technician can go
to a different house?"

00:12:15.967 --> 00:12:17.569
The Republican Party
has learned nothing,

00:12:17.569 --> 00:12:19.471
and it has not changed.
It's still the party

00:12:19.471 --> 00:12:21.507
that elected Trump
and stood by him

00:12:21.507 --> 00:12:23.075
as he attempted
to foment sedition.

00:12:23.075 --> 00:12:25.377
It's the same party
that spent eight years

00:12:25.377 --> 00:12:27.279
stonewalling
President Obama's agenda.

00:12:27.279 --> 00:12:30.382
And now, even after a historic,
resounding defeat

00:12:30.382 --> 00:12:32.485
after losing the House,
the Senate, and the presidency,

00:12:32.485 --> 00:12:35.420
Republicans are still standing
in the way of urgent relief,

00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:37.489
systemic change,
and accountability

00:12:37.489 --> 00:12:39.791
amid multiple
simultaneous crises.

00:12:39.791 --> 00:12:42.294
If you're asking yourself
what their motivation is,

00:12:42.294 --> 00:12:43.762 line:60%
it's possible that they're...
-Stupid.

00:12:43.762 --> 00:12:45.697 line:0%
This has been "A Closer Look."

